From: seilent <github@seilent.net>
Date: Fri, 29 May 2026 22:30:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8550: Add deepest idle state with system_pd

Add the deepest domain-idle-state (domain_ss3, PSCI suspend param
0x0200c354) and a system_pd power-domain above the existing cluster_pd.
Re-point cluster_pd at system_pd and apps_rsc at system_pd so RPMh
sleep/wake TCS fire from the deepest power domain when all CPUs idle.

Adapted from Maulik Shah's hamoa series:
  https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260312-hamoa_pdc-v1-4-760c8593ce50@oss.qualcomm.com

If firmware supports PSCI suspend param 0x0200c354 the SoC can reach
AOSD (Apps-Only Shutdown). Otherwise cpuidle falls back to cluster_sleep_1
which already exists.

Signed-off-by: seilent <github@seilent.net>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8550.dtsi | 23 ++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8550.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8550.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8550.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8550.dtsi
@@ -447,6 +447,14 @@
 				exit-latency-us = <4400>;
 				min-residency-us = <10150>;
 			};
+
+			domain_ss3: domain-sleep-0 {
+				compatible = "domain-idle-state";
+				arm,psci-suspend-param = <0x0200c354>;
+				entry-latency-us = <2800>;
+				exit-latency-us = <4400>;
+				min-residency-us = <9000>;
+			};
 		};
 	};
 
@@ -892,8 +900,14 @@
 
 		cluster_pd: power-domain-cluster {
 			#power-domain-cells = <0>;
+			power-domains = <&system_pd>;
 			domain-idle-states = <&cluster_sleep_0>, <&cluster_sleep_1>;
 		};
+
+		system_pd: power-domain-system {
+			#power-domain-cells = <0>;
+			domain-idle-states = <&domain_ss3>;
+		};
 	};
 
 	reserved_memory: reserved-memory {
@@ -5811,7 +5825,7 @@
 			qcom,drv-id = <2>;
 			qcom,tcs-config = <ACTIVE_TCS    3>, <SLEEP_TCS     2>,
 					  <WAKE_TCS      2>, <CONTROL_TCS   0>;
-			power-domains = <&cluster_pd>;
+			power-domains = <&system_pd>;
 
 			apps_bcm_voter: bcm-voter {
 				compatible = "qcom,bcm-voter";
